{"title":"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Proof_Format)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Proof Format)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Expanding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a21b89a270bae50817e2f5bb675aa38817a0f816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+0.2)^{1000}_{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"21\" /> by the binomial theorem and doing no further manipulation gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c14bf916c02c40e694eaa2f957cb61f108cf07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${1000 \\choose 0}(0.2)^0+{1000 \\choose 1}(0.2)^1+{1000 \\choose 2}(0.2)^2+\\cdots+{1000 \\choose 1000}(0.2)^{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"569\" height=\"55\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/1/7614a86a13eb038383bc2726776c8bf9cc6fbd24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= A_0 + A_1 + A_2 + \\cdots + A_{1000},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"240\" height=\"18\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/1778830e6f3ff2cb0cea0fad834fff9b130a1552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_k = {1000 \\choose k}(0.2)^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"158\" height=\"55\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed4ab0178cd612349fcc893da9ce1bab281f0dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 0,1,2,\\ldots,1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />. For which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bd7ae651542f61ce640fd3ca885c365f0c63e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_{}^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"13\" height=\"19\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/7/7477e41607aa79b5c8e6bfa016ab99f257d0de3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_k^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"19\" /> the largest?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Proof_Format.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Proof_Format)\">Solution 1 (Proof Format)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Proof Format)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/b/78b7b73b8f1ebf978cd5fadc957109995c3c8f21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Lemma:}$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>The \"maxima\" is the point \\( k \\) in which every \\( n &gt; k \\) results in a decrease of value.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/a/0cacfa6ee9f098c3f72226bee86478623f601790.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Conjecture:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>For all values \\( k \\) upon \\( A_k \\) there exists a value \\( n=k \\) in which \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c4ae973f1281e0f599ae5de8279a7097a77191.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{1000}{n} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^n\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>is as great as possible.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/863ec85082192d548433c901636131c5774840e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Proof of the Conjecture}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"201\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>For simplicity, denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a9ceeeb292b5b7ce24a2abc8f42c78d99008888.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = \\binom{1000}{k} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"169\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>Examine the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319b5d5be1d8567475075b755132162feacc56b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_{k+1}}{a_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"40\" height=\"37\" />. We see this simplifies into \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/911188e056a7444d6f81b1597bc0f0c68398e979.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_{k+1}}{a_k} =  \\frac{\\binom{1000}{k+1}\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^{k+1}}{\\binom{1000}{k}\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^k} = \\frac{\\binom{1000}{k+1}}{\\binom{1000}{k}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\]\" width=\"258\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>Then, the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/6/a767113592aede2bf7c0b2448850c122c1cbc847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\binom{n}{k+1}}{\\binom{n}{k}} = \\frac{n-k}{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"118\" height=\"51\" /> simplifies the above ratio as\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/0/fd0492c029302f331e6f5822cdf5564985524727.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_{k+1}}{a_k} = \\frac{1000-k}{k+1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>which can be rewritten as\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/65494e544bd3737305945d19532cbd895f5be7f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1000-k}{5(k+1)}\\]\" width=\"69\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Note that \\( 5(k+1) \\) will exponentially increase greater than \\( 1000-k \\) through properties of multiplication.\n</p><p>So, for the sequence to begin descent, we want the exact value of \\( k \\) in which\n</p><p>\\( 1000-k \\le 5(k+1) \\)\n</p><p>Solving for which we obtain\n</p><p>\\( k \\ge 165 \\frac{5}{6} \\). \n</p><p>So there exists some \\( n=k \\) for which \n</p><p>\\( \\binom{1000}{n} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^n \\)\n</p><p>is as great as possible.\n</p><p>particularly \\( n \\ge 165 \\frac{5}{6} \\)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e7358ece96f26b7a39ce4b59c5e1d839f05e3c90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Incorporation of the Conjecture}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"269\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Every term in the binomial expansion of \\( (1+0.2)^{1000} \\) must be in the form \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/399bf5cb05ee01a470778d5519e037e2d4fe51d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_k = \\binom{1000}{k}(0.2)^k\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>where \\( k \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+&#160;: 0 \\le k \\le 1000 \\).\n</p><p>The maximal value occurs at \\( k \\ge 165 \\frac{5}{6} \\). However, this isn't an integer. The next greatest integer will occur at \\( k = 166 \\). Thus the value of \\( k \\) such that \\( A_k \\) is maximized is \\(\\boxed{\\textbf{166}}\\) \\(\\square\\)\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da275a4e050ea53976a9f77372987cd9c68bf94f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x_{}^{}&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />. Then we may write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/4/83441fd28a8498c314dd2ec68d82231024609317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{k}^{}={N\\choose k}x^{k}=\\frac{N!}{k!(N-k)!}x^{k}=\\frac{(N-k+1)!}{k!}x^{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"387\" height=\"55\" />. Taking logarithms in both sides of this last equation and using the well-known fact <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e3a2b37df20ed423da820eedcf6bf5f574c251f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(a_{}^{}b)=\\log a + \\log b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" /> (valid if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec49794b42dfb384ba8856ef6143c82d2136890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{}^{},b_{}^{}&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" />), we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec7c7a81757012b852b8be2d3e340f10f297aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(A_{k})=\\log\\left[\\frac{(N-k+1)!}{k!}x^{k}\\right]=\\log\\left[\\prod_{j=1}^{k}\\frac{(N-j+1)x}{j}\\right]=\\sum_{j=1}^{k}\\log\\left[\\frac{(N-j+1)x}{j}\\right]\\, .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"674\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p>Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/b/79b8bdc9041370980d434dd910ddde3b89c25a0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(A_{k}^{})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" /> keeps increasing with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bd7ae651542f61ce640fd3ca885c365f0c63e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_{}^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"13\" height=\"19\" /> as long as the arguments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b275052b1f5ae7d9c716cdbc200e4258902d948d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(N-j+1)x}{j}&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"142\" height=\"44\" /> in each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/39208b50ee080b4ba5232ced48e9e546ad453683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log\\big[\\;\\big]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"48\" height=\"24\" /> terms (recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be32f8c965da641916c9f9b65fa14ab3112f859a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log y_{}^{} &lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"19\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b106ebb199d5fbd966cd7f21978feb4bc81a472.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;y_{}^{}&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />). Therefore, the integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bd7ae651542f61ce640fd3ca885c365f0c63e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_{}^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"13\" height=\"19\" /> that we are looking for must satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe5a2ba3ee90f7c5513e9f4983014aa50615b8f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\Big\\lfloor\\frac{(N+1)x}{1+x}\\Big\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"131\" height=\"42\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/0/0403af613fa9f77a63c23844ab2070816070066e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor z_{}^{}\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"28\" height=\"20\" /> denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ad7fe9f1a46c1c69111f6850ef89c1ea381d4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{}^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>In summary, substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45c9ae8bf227252c0a4604015dad4713be14b5ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_{}^{}=1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5eb8585c8dd4533ab0d82555cbd23436ec69b5cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{}^{}=0.2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> we finally find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa912c5b45ae9825e1c1be30b8af47ef464f8d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\boxed{166}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We know that once we have found the largest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, all values after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/7553256f94a2ce1069471dfe7c43bf8b7215ab90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/7553256f94a2ce1069471dfe7c43bf8b7215ab90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" />. Therefore, we are looking for the smallest possible value such that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a100ca48156177419af5c757fba4923523e7740.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{1}{5}}^k\\cdot {{1000} \\choose {k}}&gt;{\\frac{1}{5}}^{k+1}\\cdot {{1000} \\choose {k+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"246\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174f45af697562edef0861d545e89652372e3613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{1}{5}}^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"23\" height=\"42\" /> gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/130af935414f7456ca700b82c5e79e1ddbbf1c9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${1000\\choose k}&gt;{\\frac{1}{5}}\\cdot{1000\\choose {k+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"186\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>We can express these binomial coefficients as factorials.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e0a2d448305bf1f312d4ff49c26faa00af85849.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1000!}{(1000-k)!\\cdot(k)!}&gt;{\\frac{1}{5}}\\cdot\\frac{1000!}{(1000-k-1)!\\cdot{(k+1)!}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"383\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>We note that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54b9a3537f5b44bc4b80c957574b78df0f03fc72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> can cancel. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a2ccf5217908fc4108e5ee9b72c73d7ec6634b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1000-k)!=(1000-k)(1000-k-1)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"316\" height=\"20\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/708a5714c8fcf85b84358bb642d678a204f3d8dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+1)!=(k+1)k!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Canceling these terms yields,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/9965a6d511839efce20385c9c24041522faa68d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{(1000-k)}&gt;{\\frac{1}{5}}\\cdot\\frac{1}{(k+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"199\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Cross multiplying gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f50b4f0c3bf1fbd10f98200225c3d28e00f3474b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5k+5&gt;1000-k \\Rightarrow k&gt;165.8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"249\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, since this identity holds for all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/4085cc8b751cc211bba0bd367c9e82e399ad9610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;165.8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />, the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a816d70403b18d1a69d3a454d0153be21ed652e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{166}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/7553256f94a2ce1069471dfe7c43bf8b7215ab90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> will increase as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> increases until certain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3c5761dc26b0ed017eb9cb5531f8eab492d5638.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=m$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec38e714791f74c1d46f5e4ef24b36c8ed6474a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0 &lt; A_1 &lt; A_2 &lt; \\dots &lt; A_{m-2} &lt; A_{m-1} &lt; A_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"341\" height=\"15\" /> and  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/996ab5e1175535722e08df0466c0474793675457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_m &gt; A_{m+1} &gt; A_{m+2} &gt; \\dots &gt; A_{1000}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"275\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Next, to change <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b5a738ead41906aaff6387e13bb80461aca44e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/7553256f94a2ce1069471dfe7c43bf8b7215ab90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" />, we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b5a738ead41906aaff6387e13bb80461aca44e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/a/16a4dea6250fab7a38921eeaec1f1d3e5a5c6d4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1000-k+1}{5k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"39\" />. It follows that the numerator must be greater than the\n</p><p>denominator or\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/3/6335d6dd826fc52cc891787e7c3c3cd42803c144.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1000-k+1&gt;5k\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"14\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/4/39454df06569490d12de7e46ecfd374d42442c2c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k&lt;166.8\\]\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>We conclude that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a816d70403b18d1a69d3a454d0153be21ed652e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{166}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the expansion is the largest the moment BEFORE the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/1/3c1beac803b404bd4df8f898a6a1239d83dd84ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$nC_p &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" /> (this reasoning can probably be found in the other solutions; basically, if we have a number k and then k+1, the value is the largest when k+1 is larger than k, or in other words <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/0/cb0c232354192c8bf87179a6b73e39107a8311d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$nC_p*\\frac{1}{5} &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"94\" height=\"37\" />)\n</p><p>Say we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8ac534ebdccd69d8139319b650bd0cc04c84fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${1000 \\choose 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"60\" height=\"53\" />... this equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cd04a23266ccd86cb282f90e952b251652e1003.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1000*999*998*997*996}{5*4*3*2*1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"216\" height=\"38\" />, and if we have k+1, then it's just going to be equivalent to multiplying this fraction by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/5358b156efaa332db1905485e1336e78e27cd8be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{995}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" />. Notice that this fraction's numerator plus denominator is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888c508062c09735bab7ff0e11e7dc80cc7580db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Calling the numerator x and the denominator y, we get that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8286fc0ce4666de0e2d927653a6335a5e95372.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x+y = 1001\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b08ed6aae140facd363eb43749e0447d862deb06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x}{y} &gt; 5\\]\" width=\"45\" height=\"36\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/83119e0b90442ab7536c2a32afaea74f4545e305.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x&gt;5y\\]\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/7/db76875d5f0d2a90a29fa1b1006ae3361214c75c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6y&lt;1001\\]\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/6/e7681a2e48a8bbe9c220702aa309056055c413d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y&lt;166.83333\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" /> and since the denominator is what we are specifically choosing, or in other words what k is, we conclude k = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a816d70403b18d1a69d3a454d0153be21ed652e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{166}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>Note: It may be more intuitive to equate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/d/69d2e9c3bca929773224291a03a68b25a22a73fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> and then use test points to figure out which side of the inequality to lie on.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice the relation between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/8552538bfb66b1718ced2741732e7e6347a12aa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/2/8f21a13895c350d53406730822fd1071b3fd7632.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{m+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />. We have that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dd840b41d0ad24176685146cd24c793f0d37109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{m+1}  = A_m \\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\cdot \\frac{1000-m}{m+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"210\" height=\"39\" />. This is true because from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/8552538bfb66b1718ced2741732e7e6347a12aa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/2/8f21a13895c350d53406730822fd1071b3fd7632.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{m+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> we have to multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/6/2b626290b2a7032d57ae7c5e9021cbb29a02a0e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5}=0.2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" /> once,and then we must resolve the factorial issue. To do this, we must realize that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a873434357a090db8d1cdc039d83d3c49fc7e40.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{1000 \\choose m+1} = \\frac{1000!}{(m+1)!(1000-m-1)!} = \\frac{1000 \\cdots (1001-m)(1000-m)}{(m+1)!}\\]\" width=\"559\" height=\"53\" />\nand that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472a78d2324b2f0afe9dd0a999b3ff17c6f6e106.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{1000 \\choose m} = \\frac{1000!}{m!(1000-m)!} = \\frac{1000 \\cdots (1001-m)}{m!}\\]\" width=\"382\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706caf6e5928988a2c56ae7f949f58dc116e88c8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow {1000 \\choose m} \\cdot \\frac{1000-m}{m+1}\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>So now, we must find out for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a76f9fad6980bcc3ca3b25746dec83ed3c2bfec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000-m&lt; 5 \\cdot (m+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" /> (when this happens the numerator is less than the denominator for the fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d5f07f2575b26e03fc33d7f397096ea0e09187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1000-m}{m+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"77\" height=\"39\" /> so then we will have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/1/9e1d8c2423347e622e174e8cd11795d14864aeec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_m &gt; A_{m+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" />) Then we find that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f9e7b02d3b331e771e53b8b0427fc29b72706b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 165.833333$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"126\" height=\"13\" />, the above inequality (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a76f9fad6980bcc3ca3b25746dec83ed3c2bfec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000-m&lt; 5 \\cdot (m+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />) holds, so then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/14429e7c73b3d575d1f19db405912cf97ca783e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=165$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf77d5fe318765675ed9251812dedae38f367ea2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=m+1= \\boxed{166}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~qwertysri987\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME\" title=\"1991 AIME\">1991 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1991 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1991\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017182601\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.057 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.081 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 561/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18242/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.335      1 -total\n 58.16%    7.755      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.22%    5.230      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2908:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017182601 and revision id 270858. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}